{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`store_freshness` reports `stale-store` from a **persisted sentinel** that is never checked\nagainst observable git state. Once any ticket-branch write fails, the sentinel sticks, and\nevery plan-review and completion gate in that clone refuses to decide — permanently — even\nafter the events have demonstrably been delivered.\n\n## Observation\n\nIn `.rebar/worktrees/fix-985f-sandbox/.tickets-tracker`, after a successful manual push,\n`git rev-parse HEAD origin/tickets` printed the SAME commit\n(`9a10e59a2a825d071f5e1780dc362c7aacfb3cc2`) and `git status -sb` showed no ahead/behind.\nYet `rebar review-plan concise-deplorable-gerenuk --status` returned\n`{\"ok\": false, \"verdict\": \"stale-store\"}`, claiming \"5 committed ticket event(s) the shared\nstore has never received (last delivery failure: push-transport-failed)\". The claim of 5\nundelivered events is false, and the count is itself stale: after a later write the same\nprobe reported 1 while the refs were again level.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `src/rebar/_store/freshness.py`, `store_freshness` consults the sentinel only after the\ndivergence branch declines:\n\n```python\nstatus = push_state.read_status(tracker)\npending = status.get(\"state\") == \"pending\"\n...\nif divergence is not None:\n    ...\nelif pending:\n    verdict = \"push-pending\"\n```\n\n`_ref_divergence` (`freshness.py:66-92`) returns `None` for **both** \"level\" and \"strictly\nahead\" — its docstring says so. So when refs are level, control falls to `elif pending` and\nthe persisted sentinel decides the verdict unchallenged. The sentinel is cleared only by a\nrebar-performed push (`push.py:254`, `push.py:290`). Recovering by hand\n(`git push origin HEAD:tickets`) delivers the events and leaves the sentinel set forever.\n\n`_ref_divergence` already computes the evidence needed to falsify the sentinel; it discards\nthe level-vs-ahead distinction before the sentinel is consulted.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than tolerating\n\nThe module docstring states the design intent: \"a broken diagnostic must never be able to\nblock a healthy gate,\" and the probe deliberately degrades to `fresh` on any internal\nfailure. A false `stale-store` on a provably level store is the exact failure that contract\nexists to prevent.\n\n## Approach\n\nDistinguish **level** from **ahead** in `_ref_divergence`, and treat a level store as proof\nof delivery: when `origin/tickets` and `HEAD` are the same commit there are no undelivered\ncommitted events, so the sentinel is stale and is reconciled rather than reported.\n\n### Why level is proof for EVERY recorded reason\n\nThe marker's claim is about committed events the shared store never received, and\n`record_failure` (`push_state.py:157-176`) records it for the commit leg as well as the push\nleg — `stage-failed`, `commit-lock-timeout` and `commit-failed` are recorded DELIBERATELY,\nand in those cases HEAD is never advanced, so a marker can coexist with a level store.\nClearing is still correct there, and for the stronger reason: a write that never became a\ncommit leaves nothing to deliver, so the marker's claim is false the moment HEAD is level.\n\nClearing a commit-leg marker on delivery evidence is also not a new liberty. The same\ndocstring already states the existing rule — \"a later successful push clears the marker\neither way\" — so a commit-leg marker is already discharged by evidence unrelated to the\ncommit that failed. This change adds one more piece of evidence of the same kind.\n\n### The write, its failure behaviour, and its ownership\n\nReconciling clears the marker via `push_state.clear`, which **never raises** — it swallows\n`FileNotFoundError` and logs any other error at debug (`push_state.py:187-198`). A clear\nthat fails leaves the marker in place and the probe still returns `fresh` for that call, so\nthe fail-open contract holds by construction and no new failure mode reaches the caller.\n\nThe nearest precedent is `src/rebar/_commands/completion_delivery.py:297-301`, which clears\nonly when `local_oid == remote_oid` under the comment \"a different local HEAD can belong to\na concurrent writer whose delivery outcome we do not own\". Its comparand is NOT the same\nobject: there, `remote_oid` is the revision the remote just accepted, while the no-fetch\nprobe compares HEAD to the `origin/tickets` remote-tracking ref. The precedent taken is the\nSHAPE of the rule — clear only on exact equality, never on a merely-plausible local HEAD —\nnot the comparand.\n\nUsing the remote-tracking ref introduces no new trust: it is the same ref `_ref_divergence`\nalready uses to decide the behind and diverged verdicts. A ref that lags the true remote can\nonly understate how far ahead the local store is, and HEAD equal to that ref still means\nevery local commit is contained in a revision the remote acknowledged, so the equality\ncannot be satisfied while genuinely undelivered commits exist.\n\n### Rejected\n\n- **Clearing the sentinel on any read.** Loses the genuine push-pending signal for a clone\n  that really is ahead.\n- **Making the probe fetch.** The docstring is explicit that it is purely local and must\n  never make a gate depend on network reachability.\n- **Clearing only for push-leg reasons.** A commit-leg marker on a level store wedges every\n  gate just as hard, and the marker's claim is false in that case too.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A regression test drives a tracker into `push_state` pending, brings HEAD level with\n      `origin/tickets`, and asserts `store_freshness` returns verdict `fresh`, added to\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py`.\n- [x] That same test is recorded failing on baseline `main`, with the `stale-store` verdict\n      quoted on this ticket.\n- [x] A clone genuinely AHEAD of `origin/tickets` with the sentinel set still reports\n      `push-pending`, asserted by its own test so the fix cannot whitewash undelivered events.\n- [x] A level store whose marker records the commit-leg reason `commit-failed` also reports\n      `fresh`, asserted by its own test.\n- [x] The existing cases in `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py` pass unchanged,\n      covering behind via `test_a_store_behind_the_shared_store_is_stale`, diverged via\n      `test_a_diverged_store_is_stale`, and fail-open via\n      `test_the_probe_fails_OPEN_on_its_own_error`.\n- [x] After one level-store probe, a second `push_state.read_status` call reports state `ok`,\n      asserted in the same test.\n- [x] When `push_state.clear` cannot remove the marker, the probe still returns `fresh`,\n      asserted by its own test.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The full verify suite is green for this change, with the run and its\n      exit code recorded on this ticket. The authoritative signal is the Gerrit `Verified`\n      vote on this change's patch set, which runs the same selection `make test` runs.\n      provenance: environment=github-actions-hosted-runner; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — CI run 35488604462 executed the gating suite against Gerrit change 2990 patch set 1 (revision 2f22eef69e373ec74b2521fe3404740cc0f66c32) and concluded SUCCESS, casting `Verified +1`; that run is the same merge gate that admits the change to `main`, so its exit status is the authoritative verify result rather than a simulation of one.\n\n## Testing\n\n`pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py` covers the ref states (level, ahead, behind,\ndiverged) crossed with the sentinel set and unset, both a push-leg and a commit-leg recorded\nreason, the reconciliation assertion that a second `push_state.read_status` reports state\n`ok`, and the fail-open assertion that a failing clear still yields `fresh`. `make verify` is\nthe pre-push gate and must exit 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789882688985388309,"uuid":"09b02923-a95d-4a56-b03b-5742781aa608"}